  "summary": "OpenAI is deepening its healthcare footprint by connecting ChatGPT directly to Epic EHRs and launching its new GPT-6 Astra model, while concerns about AI accountability in medicine persist—particularly around whether physicians should bear responsibility for AI-generated clinical decisions without meaningful oversight. The sector is experiencing significant consolidation, with digital health M&A accelerating as companies like Vitality (acquiring Icario), Cureety (acquiring Reimagine Care), and others pursue growth, while major funding rounds for AI-focused startups like Elucid ($55M), Konko AI ($6M), and Scan.com ($220M) signal investor confidence in specialized clinical AI. Healthcare organizations are simultaneously grappling with critical infrastructure challenges: cybersecurity vulnerabilities are widening as McKesson and others report data breaches, while EHR implementation struggles persist, including a House subpoena over Oracle's massive cost overruns at the VA. Hospitals are investing in AI governance and audit trails now, with institutions like Ochsner Health establishing dedicated innovation leadership to manage safe AI deployment, and the industry is beginning to rethink reimbursement models and documentation standards to accommodate AI-augmented workflows.",
